Thu Nov 26 09:18:23 UTC 2026 - Jordi Relats <4889953+jordirelats@users.noreply.github.com>

- Update to 0.5.1, fixes from a review from six points of view and:
  * Help in English, Catalan, German and French (F1), with links that
    open each section, and About with the version, credits and license
  * Packages and Discover by theme: mark several and install, remove or
    lock them at once
  * Updates in parts: every part is tried with zypper before anything
    is installed; packages that need a decision wait for the final dup,
    which only runs if every part worked; a small update can still run
    when only the safety margin is missing
  * Many problems: "leave them as they are" locks what must stay
    together in one round, says which Tumbleweed packages it holds back,
    and Locks shows those locks with a button to unlock them; only
    repositories rebuilt for Tumbleweed count as "not up to date yet"
  * Opened .rpm files are installed from a private copy, and unsigned
    files (bridges first) get commands of their own
  * Keys are linked to a repository only when that is known for sure,
    with the whole fingerprint shown
  * The tray icon stays off for whoever turned it off, restarts itself
    after an upgrade, and the reminder works without the window
  * Sidebar fits small windows (Help and About under it), the problem
    window and the questions fit small screens, big queues stay fast
  * A rare crash (Python's collector in a worker thread) is fixed
  * Recommends fwupd and xdg-utils, suggests snapper

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Thu Nov 26 07:45:00 UTC 2026 - Jordi Relats <4889953+jordirelats@users.noreply.github.com>

- Update to 0.5.0:
  * Every question that changes the system says what will be done in
    plain words, what it means for you, and shows the exact commands
    underneath as information; Enter never starts a change
  * The queue review has a button per change, shows which change needs
    which, and asks before taking out something others need; after a
    failed step only what was really done leaves the queue
  * A big upgrade asks whether it is worth waiting (size, how new the
    Tumbleweed version is, battery) and can only download it or remind
    you tomorrow from the tray icon
  * Little disk space: the upgrade can run in parts that zypper
    resolves and downloads completely before installing them, after
    freeing the package cache and old kernels
  * Many dependency problems are grouped by cause (a repository not yet
    rebuilt for the new Tumbleweed, packages that no longer exist,
    locks), with wait, leave them as they are, or one by one
  * Failed downloads right after a new Tumbleweed explain that the
    mirrors are still copying it
  * RPMs made for Fedora whose requirements openSUSE has under other
    names get a small bridge package, written without rpm-build, with a
    list of bridges that says when one is no longer needed
  * Repositories that programs leave in /etc/yum.repos.d, which zypper
    ignores, can be added to zypper with their key
  * The tray icon that tells about updates starts at login from the
    package itself (/etc/xdg/autostart), without opening the window
    first; it can be turned off per user in Settings
  * The version is shown in the window title

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Thu Nov 26 08:00:00 UTC 2026 - Jordi Relats <4889953+jordirelats@users.noreply.github.com>

- Update to 0.4.1, fixes from a review (security, zypper, code,
  interface, language, packaging):
  * Solutions chosen in the dup window run as one 'zypper install'
    transaction that refuses instead of removing what depends on a
    package; the dup window's default button simulates
  * Removals and installs of the queue are simulated and applied as one
    transaction; --no-clean-deps when not asked for
  * Signing key import: exactly one key block, re-exported from a
    throwaway keyring before rpm sees it; vendors' next keys are not
    offered for deletion; Search online queues keys instead of importing
  * Repository address changes add the new repository before removing
    the old one and keep every setting (gpgkey included); "--" before
    every alias
  * The refresh timer follows the wall clock (laptops that suspend),
    downloads ahead only on AC power, and the window says when zypper is
    busy with it; fwupdmgr never uploads reports by itself
  * Unlocking locks with a version range or a repository works; History
    warns that /opt and other subvolumes are not in snapshots
  * The window warns when the root helper is older than the app
  * Faster Applications page, pages fit 1100x700, cleaner package card,
    consistent counts, many wording and translation fixes

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Nov 25 22:30:00 UTC 2026 - Jordi Relats <4889953+jordirelats@users.noreply.github.com>

- Update to 0.4.0:
  * Tray icon with a daily notification about updates (repositories,
    Flatpak, programs from the web, firmware), and a system timer
    (zypp-desk-refresh.timer) that refreshes the repositories as root
    and never installs anything
  * Firmware updates through fwupd in the Updates page
  * History with snapper snapshots: compare the files, undo a change,
    keep the snapshot you started from
  * Choose one of zypper's solutions to a dependency problem
  * Signing keys page: see who signs what, delete unused keys, import
    keys from a web address, a file or a fingerprint
  * zypp.conf settings, written to /etc/zypp/zypp.conf.d/50-zypp-desk.conf
  * Graphical routine editor
  * Repository priorities on the cards, a suggested order, and a new
    address for a repository that moved
  * Open downloaded RPM files (Zypp Desk is one more application for
    application/x-rpm), and only one window at a time
  * Remove also what only a package needed (--clean-deps)

